<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- OstrichChallenge: the check-in bell.
     The vanilla elevator_ding plays through AudioSource_Interact, the quiet source used for
     door handles and switches, so it was easy to miss. This plays the first ding clip (Fril's pick of the four)
     through AudioSource_VO_Announce, the source the traders use for their announcements, which
     is made to be heard clearly. The mod plays it to the player twice, a "ding-ding", on every wave.

     v1.26.0: THE OLD COMMENT HERE CLAIMED "It has NO Noise entry, so it never attracts zombies or
     the stalker", while the node below set NoiseScale to 1 and CrouchNoiseScale to 0.5. That was
     never verified. Fril, 2 October, having seen it twice: "The guests bell ... is being played at
     my location, by me, and its very loud. Twice now its woken sleepers that are nearby."

     He is right that it plays at his location: Audio.Manager.PlayInsidePlayerHead parents the
     AudioSource to the local player's transform and sets its position to the player's. That method
     never calls SignalAI, so on the code that can be read it should emit no AI noise, and the
     mechanism is NOT proven. But an explicit zero costs nothing and a claim in a comment is worth
     nothing, so both scales are now 0 rather than absent. Absent means "whatever the default is".
     Zero means zero.

     IF THE BELL STILL WAKES SLEEPERS after this, the SoundDataNode is not the cause and the next
     two candidates are the world ding rung at reception (Audio.Manager.BroadcastPlay, vanilla's own
     elevator_ding1, whose noise properties this mod does not control) and the eight entrance doors
     the mod forces open on the same tick. Neither is at the player, so neither fits the symptom as
     described, which is why they are second and third rather than first. -->
<configs>
    <!-- v2.0.0: removes only the mod's OWN radio nodes, so a reinstall is idempotent.
         The xpath is deliberately narrow: it cannot match occArmouryAlarm or occupancyBell. -->
    <remove xpath="/Sounds/SoundDataNode[starts-with(@name, 'occRadio')]" />

    <append xpath="/Sounds">

        <!-- v1.89.0: THE ARMOURY CHEST ALARM. Vanilla's own alarm clip, deliberately WITHOUT
             Loop="true" (vanilla's alarm1 has it, alarm1_oneshot does not): Alarm.cs plays this
             again every couple of seconds for thirty, so the burst ends by running out rather
             than by something having to find and stop a looping AudioSource.
             AudioSource_VO_Announce is the loud source, the same one the check-in bell uses
             after the quiet Interact source turned out to be easy to miss.
             The Noise element is copied from vanilla's alarm_house_biz_lp1 so the figures are
             vanilla's rather than invented. Alarm.cs ALSO calls AIDirector.NotifyNoise with the
             player as instigator, because the mod's own hearing model ignores any noise whose
             instigator is not an EntityPlayer. -->
        <SoundDataNode name="occArmouryAlarm"> <AudioSource name="@:Sounds/Prefabs/AudioSource_VO_Announce.prefab"/>
            <Noise ID="4" noise="60" time="2" heat_map_strength="0.2" heat_map_time="90"/>
            <AudioClip ClipName="@:Sounds/Electricity/Alarms/alarm1_lp.wav"/>
            <LocalCrouchVolumeScale value="1.0"/> <CrouchNoiseScale value="0.5"/> <NoiseScale value="1"/> <MaxVoices value="10"/> <MaxRepeatRate value="0"/>
        </SoundDataNode>

        <SoundDataNode name="occupancyBell"> <AudioSource name="@:Sounds/Prefabs/AudioSource_VO_Announce.prefab"/>
            <AudioClip ClipName="@:Sounds/TriggeredEvents/elevator_ding1.wav"/>
            <LocalCrouchVolumeScale value="1.0"/> <CrouchNoiseScale value="0"/> <NoiseScale value="0"/> <MaxVoices value="10"/> <MaxRepeatRate value="0"/>
        </SoundDataNode>
    

        <!-- ===========================================================================
             v2.0.0, 9 Oct 2026: THE RADIO BROADCASTS. 80 clips across 14 SoundDataNodes.

             THIS FILE ALREADY EXISTED AND I OVERWROTE IT. The bell and the alarm above were
             destroyed by a blind write at 22:27 and recovered from the v1.99.2 zip twenty
             minutes later, only because Fril asked "Does the sounds you just sent me include
             the occupancyBell and the ArmouryAlarm??". Shipped, it would have silenced the
             check-in bell, which the entire night cycle hangs off, and the armoury alarm.
             CHECK WHETHER A CONFIG EXISTS BEFORE WRITING ONE. Appending is the default; a
             fresh file is the exception and needs the old one read first.

             COPIED FROM A WORKING EXAMPLE, NOT INVENTED. The structure below is lifted from
             Frils_Drone_Voices_Mod's Sounds.xml, which loads today: the vanilla
             AudioSource_VO.prefab, the "#@modfolder:Resources/<bundle>.unity3d?<folder>/<clip>"
             ClipName form with no extension, and one folder per key inside the bundle.

             RANDOM SELECTION IS FREE. Vanilla's own sounds.xml documents it: "a wave file to
             play at random when this SoundDataNode is called. Multiple entries will add to the
             list of possible sounds to play." 1081 vanilla nodes work this way. So Radio.cs asks
             for "occRadioTwo" and the game picks one of the six.

             IT DOES NOT GIVE US Fril's "never repeated": vanilla random can hand you the same
             clip twice running. Accepted for now. If it grates, the fix is one node per TAKE and
             the choosing moved into Radio.cs, and no recording changes.

             TWO DELIBERATE DIFFERENCES FROM THE DRONE:
               MaxVoices is 1, not 10. A drone can talk over itself; a broadcast must not.
               NO <Noise> NODE. The drone's is noise="7", audible to the AI. A radio that draws
               the stalker to the roof is a real idea and might be a good one, but it is a
               GAMEPLAY change nobody asked for. Left out and flagged rather than slipped in.
             =========================================================================== -->
